		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see How to use <strong>Factories</strong> (Factories / seeder) in Laravel 8, with the use of the Factory class and combine it with the faker library, to test test data, we will use PostgreSQL and the graphical interface pgAdmin 4..</p>

		<h2>How do factories work in laravel 8?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 	
		
		<p>First we have to create the class with which we are going to work <code>php artisan make:factory Project
		</code>, once created with the Factory created <strong>Factory created successfully</strong>, we will have a class with a <code>definition()</code> method, which we are going to combine with the <strong>faker</strong> libray to work with test data, remember to preload the migrations <code>php artisan migrate</code>.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		namespace Database\Factories;

		use App\Models\Project;
		use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Factories\Factory;

		class ProjectFactory extends Factory
		{
		    /**
		     * The name of the factory's corresponding model.
		     *
		     * @var string
		     */
		    protected $model = Project::class;

		    /**
		     * Define the model's default state.
		     *
		     * @return array
		     */
		    public function definition()
		    {
		    	// define the methods of the facker library
		        return [
		         'client_name' => $this->faker->name(),
		         'client_company_name' => $this->faker->company(),
		         'client_phone' => $this->faker->phoneNumber(),
		         'client_email' => $this->faker->companyEmail(),
		         'client_address' => $this->faker->address(),
		         'project_name' => $this->faker->jobTitle(),
		     ];
		 }
		}
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>Now in the archive <code>DatabaseSeeder.php</code>, add as a parameter to the factory class the set of values that we are going to insert in the associated table, in this case they would be <strong>30</strong>, we now execute the command <code>php artisan db:seed</code> to insert the data.</p>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		namespace Database\Seeders;

		use Illuminate\Database\Seeder;


		class DatabaseSeeder extends Seeder
		{
		    /**
		     * Seed the application's database.
		     *
		     * @return void
		     */
		    public function run()
		    {        
		    	// we will add this line of code
		        \App\Models\Project::factory(30)->create();
		        
		    }
		}
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>Result in our table with the use of PostgreSQL and pgAdmin 4, we have generated 30 records with random data with the faker library.</p>

